{"id": "swebq0077", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3903150144, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "what type of government does the us constitution set up?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0077.wav", "input_sha256": "96e0c441edc20dafd53305c61721e09d26f04fb10f02f32de69a9acfba9c216b", "input_samples": 67598, "input_s": 4.225, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.222, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The U.S. Constitution sets up a federal government with three branch es, the executive, legislative and judicial. Each branch has specific responsibilities and they are designed to check and balance each other, preventing any one from having too much power. So it' s not just one type of government but a system meant to keep things fair and balanced.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 19, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0077_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "dcad6e11de79b3fadc424c4abc73f92bf65c94e192a51b507c5a401ae8def76d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 19.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.073, 1.131, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.076, 2.135, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.077, 3.137, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.076, 4.138, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 4.225, 4.297, 4.935, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.225, 5.299, 5.979, 0, 24000, 0], [6, 0, 6.225, 6.297, 6.932, 0, 24000, 0], [7, 0, 7.225, 7.30