{"id": "swebq0208", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 887031672, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "what kind of guitar did george harrison use?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0208.wav", "input_sha256": "b8838eb4e6964218aef82924b8480e6d57099f7c34e97ff91c05fb7236787ae9", "input_samples": 38620, "input_s": 2.414, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.6505, "act": 0.9993, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "George Harrison used many guitars throughout his career, but some of his most famous were: Rickenbacker 360/12 — a 12-string electric guitar heavily associated with early Beatles songs like “A Hard Day’s Night.” , Gretsch Country Gentleman — one of his main early Beatles guitars. , Gretsch Duo Jet — one of his first important electric guitars. , Fender Stratocaster “Rocky” — a psychedelic-painted Strat he used in the mid-to-late Beatles era. , Gibson SG — used around the Revolver period. , Fender Telecaster — notably the rosewood Telecaster used during the Let It Be sessions and rooftop concert.", "expert_answer": "George Harrison used **many guitars** throughout his career, but some of his most famous were:\n\n- **Rickenbacker 360/12** — a 12-string electric guitar heavily associated with early Beatles songs like “A Hard Day’s Night.”\n- **Gretsch Country Gentleman** — one of his main early Beatles guitars.\n- **Gretsch Duo Jet** — one of his first important electric guitars.\n- **Fender Stratocaster “Rocky”** — a psychedelic-painted Strat he used in the mid-to-late Beatles era.\n- **Gibson SG** — used around the *Revolver* period.\n- **Fender Telecaster** — notably the rosewood 